@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# EXEC0253 — Classic controller command availability (not original first Spring)
+
+Inherited, complete native C11 source: EXEC0252. This increment repairs the live 1280x720 command menu in gk1_native_shell.c; it had marked Classic TAX `LOCKED` although its existing source-authenticated controller route actually supports manual-derived Tax-rate actions. The new source-authored gk134_menu_capability classifies all 14 commands, distinguishes quoted Trade prices from real merchants, and changes PASS to ENDED after orders are exhausted. After exactly three Classic actions but before irreversible Pass, TAX and ASSIGN display `UNDO ONLY` so the existing Y-port-undo path remains discoverable.
+
+No original country record or ROM is embedded/changed. All changes are presentation only. The source/derived integrity gate remains in the existing dispatcher. This does NOT implement independent original first Spring, original 6502 RNG/history, an actual merchant encounter, subsequent seasons, AI, diplomacy, dynasty or full battles. Original fresh Mongol WorkRAM evidence and archived Mongol/World SaveRAM evidence remain distinct and private.
+
+Reproduction: CMake configure, build and ctest against source/execution_199. With zlib required, the 215/215 full Release native Linux CTest suite passes. Owner-private original source is required for an on-screen original command menu; generic Xvfb smoke cannot prove that visual path.
